  "Terraform State": makeSections([
    r("Terraform state configuration and real infrastructure madhya mapping maintain chestundi. Terraform resources ni identify cheyyadaniki idi important.", "Terraform state records the relationship between configuration addresses and real infrastructure objects, along with metadata needed for future operations."),
    r("Terraform state refresh and planning time lo provider data tho reconcile avuthundi; state resource identity and attributes maintain chestundi.", "Terraform uses state to track managed object identities and attributes, compare infrastructure with configuration, and determine which operations are required."),
    r("Team remote backend use chesi shared state maintain chestundi, locking enable chesi concurrent production applies prevent chestundi.", "A team stores production state in a protected remote backend so authorized engineers and CI jobs can coordinate changes without overwriting one another."),
    r("State file, backend, state locking, lineage, serial number, resource instances, and sensitive attributes state management lo important.", "State management involves the state file, backend, locking mechanism, resource instances, lineage, serial metadata, and potentially sensitive stored attributes."),
    r("Backend select chesi initialize cheyyali, state access verify cheyyali, locking confirm cheyyali, backup and recovery procedure test cheyyali.", "Configure a suitable backend, initialize the working directory, verify access and locking behavior, protect backups, and test recovery procedures."),
    r("Commands: terraform state list, terraform state show, terraform state pull, terraform state mv, terraform state rm.", "State inspection commands include terraform state list and show. Pull, move, and remove operations require extra care because they can affect Terraform's tracking data."),
    r("Remote backend configuration lo backend type and required settings declare chestaru; credentials secure identity dwara provide cheyyali.", "A backend block selects the remote storage mechanism and required settings. Authentication should come from secure identity configuration rather than embedded secrets."),
    r("State file ni Git lo commit cheyyadam, manually edit cheyyadam, locking disable cheyyadam, and backup lekunda replace cheyyadam risky.", "Common mistakes include committing state to source control, manually editing state, disabling locking, sharing unrestricted access, and changing backend settings without migration planning."),
    r("State mismatch vaste backend location, workspace, lock status, resource IDs, recent applies, and backup consistency inspect cheyyali.", "Troubleshoot state problems by confirming the backend and workspace, checking active locks, reviewing recent operations, validating object IDs, and comparing protected backups."),
    r("Remote encrypted backend, locking, versioning, least privilege, backup retention, and documented state recovery process use cheyyali.", "Use encrypted remote storage, supported locking, access controls, versioned backups, audit logs, and a documented recovery procedure for state corruption or loss."),
    r("State sensitive values store cheyyachu. State read permission kuda restrict cheyyali; encryption alone access control ki replacement kaadu.", "State may contain secrets or sensitive infrastructure metadata. Restrict read access as carefully as write access, and combine encryption with strong authorization."),
    r("State is Terraform tracking database. Configuration desired state describe chestundi; state existing managed object identities track chestundi.", "Configuration describes the desired infrastructure, while state tracks Terraform's managed object identities and recorded attributes. State is not a substitute for configuration."),
    r("Backend, State Locking, Workspace, Resource Address, Terraform Import, and Terraform Plan related concepts.", "Related concepts include backends, state locking, workspaces, resource addresses, import workflows, refresh behavior, and Terraform plans."),
  ]),

  "Terraform Module": makeSections([
    r("Terraform module reusable infrastructure configuration package. Repeated resource definitions ni organized and consistent ga maintain cheyyadaniki use chestaru.", "A Terraform module is a collection of Terraform configuration files that can be reused to provision a defined set of infrastructure resources."),
    r("Root module child modules ni call chestundi. Inputs variables dwara pass avuthayi and outputs useful values parent module ki return chestayi.", "A root module can call child modules, pass input variables, and consume outputs. Module sources can be local paths or supported remote sources."),
    r("Organization standard VPC module create chesi development, staging, production environments lo reuse chestundi.", "An organization maintains a reviewed networking module that creates standard VPC components and reuses it with different CIDR ranges and environment inputs."),
    r("Module structure lo main.tf, variables.tf, outputs.tf, versions.tf, README, examples, and optional tests untayi.", "A maintainable module commonly includes resource definitions, input variables, outputs, provider requirements, documentation, examples, and automated tests."),
    r("Module create cheyyali, inputs and outputs define cheyyali, root module nunchi call cheyyali, validate and plan chesi apply cheyyali.", "Create the module, define its inputs and outputs, reference its source from the root module, pass required values, and validate the resulting plan."),
    r("Commands: terraform init, terraform get, terraform validate, terraform plan, terraform providers.", "Use terraform init to download module dependencies, terraform get when needed to fetch modules, and validate and plan to inspect module configuration."),
    r("Module block lo source and version specify cheyyachu; required inputs arguments ga pass cheyyachu.", "A module block identifies the source and, for supported remote sources, a version or revision. Required input variables are passed as named arguments."),
    r("Hardcoded environment values, unclear inputs, missing outputs, circular module dependencies, and unpinned remote sources common mistakes.", "Common mistakes include hardcoded environment settings, poorly named variables, missing outputs, circular dependencies, and using mutable remote module references."),
    r("Module error vaste source path, required variables, provider requirements, module version, and downloaded dependency files inspect cheyyali.", "Troubleshoot module failures by checking the source path, required inputs, provider constraints, module version, initialization output, and dependency compatibility."),
    r("Small focused modules create cheyyali, inputs validate cheyyali, README maintain cheyyali, and module releases version cheyyali.", "Keep modules focused, validate inputs, document examples and outputs, test changes, and publish immutable versioned releases for shared use."),
    r("Module code lo credentials hardcode cheyyakudadhu. Secure provider authentication and narrow resource permissions enforce cheyyali.", "Do not embed credentials in modules. Use secure provider authentication, least-privilege permissions, and safe defaults for network and storage resources."),
    r("Module abstraction reuse and consistency improve chestundi, kani excessive nesting debugging and maintenance difficult chestundi.", "Modules improve reuse and consistency, but excessive abstraction or deeply nested module calls can make dependency flow and troubleshooting difficult."),
    r("Terraform Resource, Variable, Output, Provider, Registry, and Root Module related concepts.", "Related concepts include resources, variables, outputs, providers, module registries, root modules, child modules, and semantic versioning."),
