    r("Project lo webservers, appservers, and dbservers groups create chesi each group ki separate playbook tasks apply chestaru.", "A project groups web, application, and database servers separately so playbooks can target the correct systems and apply group-specific variables."),
    r("Inventory file, hosts, groups, child groups, host variables, group variables, and dynamic inventory plugins main components.", "Inventory structure includes hosts, parent and child groups, host variables, group variables, inventory plugins, and connection settings."),
    r("Hosts define cheyyali, groups organize cheyyali, variables assign cheyyali, ansible-inventory output verify chesi connectivity test cheyyali.", "Define hosts, organize them into groups, assign required variables, inspect the parsed inventory, and test connectivity before running a playbook."),
    r("Commands: ansible-inventory -i inventory.ini --list, --graph, ansible all -i inventory.ini -m ping.", "Use ansible-inventory --list to inspect parsed data, --graph to view group relationships, and the ping module to test host connectivity."),
    r("INI example lo [webservers] group kinda server addresses list cheyyachu; YAML inventory lo all.children structure use cheyyachu.", "An INI inventory can list hosts under groups such as webservers. YAML inventory represents the hierarchy through all, children, hosts, and vars keys."),
    r("Wrong host aliases, invalid group names, incorrect YAML nesting, and conflicting variables inventory targeting mistakes create chestayi.", "Common mistakes include incorrect host addresses, malformed YAML hierarchy, misspelled group names, conflicting variables, and unexpected default inventory selection."),
    r("Host target avvakapothe inventory path, parsed --list output, group membership, host pattern, and SSH variables inspect cheyyali.", "When hosts are skipped, verify the inventory path, parsed host list, group membership, playbook host pattern, connection variables, and SSH reachability."),
    r("Separate environment inventories maintain cheyyali, group variables use cheyyali, dynamic inventory sources validate cheyyali.", "Maintain clear environment-specific inventories, centralize shared settings in group variables, validate dynamic discovery, and avoid duplicating host definitions."),
    r("Inventory lo credentials plaintext ga store cheyyakudadhu. Secrets Vault or approved secret manager lo store cheyyali.", "Do not store plaintext passwords or private keys in inventory. Use Ansible Vault or an approved secret manager and restrict inventory repository access."),
    r("Inventory determines where playbooks run; playbook tasks determine what operations are performed on matched hosts.", "Inventory selects target hosts and provides connection metadata. The playbook defines the tasks executed on those selected hosts."),
