    r("Playbook role ni include chestundi; Ansible role directory conventions follow ayi required tasks and assets load chestundi.", "A playbook references a role, and Ansible loads its conventional directories to execute tasks and access defaults, templates, files, and handlers."),
    r("Organization common nginx role maintain chesi multiple environments lo installation, configuration, and service management standardize chestundi.", "A team maintains an Nginx role that installs the package, renders a configuration template, enables the service, and reuses it across web-server groups."),
    r("Role folders lo tasks, handlers, templates, files, vars, defaults, meta, and optional tests untayi.", "A standard role can contain tasks, handlers, templates, files, vars, defaults, metadata, and tests, with each directory serving a defined purpose."),
    r("Role skeleton create chesi defaults and tasks define cheyyali, handlers and templates add cheyyali, playbook nunchi invoke chesi test cheyyali.", "Create the role structure, define defaults and tasks, add required templates and handlers, reference the role in a playbook, and test it against controlled hosts."),
    r("Command: ansible-galaxy role init nginx_role. Run with ansible-playbook and inspect role files and task output.", "Use ansible-galaxy role init to generate a role skeleton, then run a playbook that references the role and inspect its execution results."),
